00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.550
When working with Word documents,
there may be occasions where

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:05.880
you need to change a specific
word or words within a document.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:09.600
If the document is only one page long,
that can be quite straightforward

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.870
and you can just go through
and replace each word manually.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:17.250
However, when working with large
documents, it may be a case that this

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.380
is unrealistic and time-consuming.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.730
Within Word, there is a feature called
find and replace, which would allow

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:27.180
you to search for specific words and
then replace them with another word.

00:00:28.425 --> 00:00:31.425
In this example letter that I
have on the screen, I'm going to

00:00:31.425 --> 00:00:36.075
find the word "information" and
replace that with the word "data".

00:00:36.945 --> 00:00:41.085
I know there are several instances of
the word information, so to access the

00:00:41.085 --> 00:00:46.485
find and replace tool, I simply go to
the edit menu button, scroll down to

00:00:46.485 --> 00:00:49.815
select find and then select replace.

00:00:50.475 --> 00:00:53.025
This brings up the find
and replace dialogue box.

00:00:53.955 --> 00:00:56.505
So the word I'm looking
for is "information".

00:00:57.765 --> 00:01:01.004
And it will highlight every instance
of the word information and I'm

00:01:01.004 --> 00:01:03.285
going to change that with "data".

00:01:04.455 --> 00:01:08.804
So once I'm happy, if I select
Replace All that will automatically

00:01:08.804 --> 00:01:14.804
replace every instance of the word
"information" with the word "data".

